\title{Category Madness}
\taxon{Root}
\meta{layer}{human}
\tag{index}

\p{A Lean 4 library of category theory whose only primitive is the virtual double ∞-category (\ref{dec-rt-0001}): ordinary categories, ∞-categories, enriched and internal categories, and equipments are instances of one definition, and every theorem is proved once against a sealed interface (\ref{dec-ch-0001}, \ref{dec-rt-0013}). Working name \em{Category Madness}, after the repository; the design documents left the name TBD.}

\p{This forest is the primary human-facing document and the bookkeeping system (\ref{dec-wf-0001}…\ref{dec-wf-0007}). The phase −1 design documents were ported into it at \ref{ms-0000} and are frozen as history under \code{design/}; the port is described in \ref{wf-0001}. Every decision, acceptance test, open question and milestone is a node; generated nodes for Lean declarations (\ref{dec-wf-0001}) will join them under \code{build/forest/} once there is Lean.}

\subtree{
  \title{How to read}
  \ul{
    \li{\ref{ch-0000} — principles, the three-stage bootstrap, the seal, layering. Read first.}
    \li{\ref{krn-0000} — stage 0: mathlib scaffolding, shape categories, patterns, Reedy/EZ, Kan machinery.}
    \li{\ref{rt-0000} — stage 1: the VDC∞ definition, \code{Mod}/\code{Mat}, \code{Category} as an instance, the seal.}
    \li{\ref{up-0000} — terminal objects, slices, limits, Kan extensions, witnesses.}
    \li{\ref{ft-0000} — augmented virtual ∞-equipments and formal category theory.}
    \li{\ref{sp-0000} — universe, the Segal category of spaces, \code{Mat(Kan)}, ∞-operads.}
    \li{\ref{tl-0000} — generated APIs, attributes, tactics, the seal linter.}
    \li{\ref{wf-0000} — forest, generated nodes, decision registry, retrieval MCP, agent loop.}
    \li{\ref{rm-0000} — milestones, freezes, acceptance criteria, risk register.}
    \li{\ref{bib-0000} — annotated references keyed to decisions.}
    \li{\ref{rev-0000} — the adversarial pass on the design and how each item was disposed into decisions.}
  }
}

\subtree{
  \title{Conventions}
  \ul{
    \li{\strong{Decisions} carry IDs \code{D-<AREA>-<nn>} (CH charter, KR kernel, RT root, UP universal properties, FT formal theory, SP spaces, TL tooling, WF workflow, RM roadmap) and live at \code{dec-<area>-<nnnn>}. Each has \em{Decision / Rationale / Rejected / Acceptance / Status}.}
    \li{\strong{Status} is \code{frozen} (changes require a superseding decision), \code{provisional} (agents may propose amendments, see \ref{dec-tl-0001}), or \code{later} (not before the stated milestone). A superseded decision is never edited; it gets \code{superseded-by}.}
    \li{\strong{Acceptance tests} carry IDs \code{AT-<AREA>-<n>} at \code{at-<area>-<nnnn>}. An acceptance test is a Lean statement (or a small family of them) whose proof is the evidence that a definition is right. Status \code{unstated} / \code{stated} / \code{proved} (\ref{dec-wf-0003}).}
    \li{\strong{Open questions} for the human carry IDs \code{OQ-<AREA>-<n>} at \code{oq-<area>-<nnnn>}.}
    \li{\strong{Milestones} \code{M0}…\code{M7} live at \code{ms-0000}…\code{ms-0007}; phase −1 is \ref{ms-design}.}
    \li{Mathematical claims marked \strong{(verify)} are expected but not yet checked against the literature or by proof; they are tasks, not facts.}
  }
}

